generation.prompt:
A 9-site spin-1/2 chain in a random longitudinal field is governed by H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{7} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{i+1} - h * sum_{i=0}^{8} sigma^x_i - sum_{i=0}^{8} epsilon_i sigma^z_i, with J = 1, open boundary conditions, and fixed quenched disorder values epsilon = {0.11, -0.19, 0.08, 0.22, -0.14, 0.17, -0.09, 0.20, -0.13} (drawn from Uniform[-0.25, 0.25], seed 42). Sweep h/J from 0.10 to 3.00 in steps of 0.10 (30 parameter points). Unlike the clean TFIM, the random field explicitly breaks the Z2 symmetry at each site, converting the true phase transition into a crossover. Design observables that detect this disorder-rounded crossover and estimate the pseudo-critical field h_pseudo. Study how the disorder affects: (a) the width and height of the susceptibility peak compared to the clean case, (b) the local magnetization profile <sigma^z_i> for each site at h/J = 1.0 (which will be spatially inhomogeneous due to disorder), (c) the correlation length estimated from C(r) = <sigma^z_0 sigma^z_r>, and (d) the distribution of local susceptibilities chi_i = d<sigma^z_i>/dh. Additionally, run the same simulation with epsilon_i = 0 (clean limit) at the same parameter points and report the quantitative differences in peak width and height. Use N_shots = 8192. Report: estimated_critical_point (pseudo-critical h_pseudo from susceptibility peak for the disordered system), critical_point_error (|h_pseudo - 1.0| for the disordered realization vs. the clean system), observable_accuracy (comparison of all chosen observables against classical exact diagonalization), phase_classification_accuracy (crossover region classification), and noise_aware_performance (effect of shot noise on h_pseudo estimation in the absence of a sharp transition).

Task inputs:
{
  "physical_system": "1D random-field transverse Ising model (RFTIM), 9 sites, open boundary conditions, disorder-rounded transition",
  "num_spins": 9,
  "hamiltonian": {
    "expression": "H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{7} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{i+1} - h * sum_{i=0}^{8} sigma^x_i - sum_{i=0}^{8} epsilon_i * sigma^z_i",
    "parameters": {
      "J": 1.0,
      "h": "swept",
      "epsilon_i": "quenched disorder: specific realization given below"
    },
    "disorder_realization": {
      "seed": 42,
      "disorder_strength": "W = 0.25 (uniform distribution on [-W, W])",
      "values": {
        "epsilon_0": 0.11,
        "epsilon_1": -0.19,
        "epsilon_2": 0.08,
        "epsilon_3": 0.22,
        "epsilon_4": -0.14,
        "epsilon_5": 0.17,
        "epsilon_6": -0.09,
        "epsilon_7": 0.2,
        "epsilon_8": -0.13
      }
    },
    "boundary_conditions": "open",
    "matrix_dimension": 512
  },
  "parameter_sweep": {
    "parameter": "h/J",
    "values": "0.10, 0.20, 0.30, ..., 3.00",
    "num_points": 30,
    "step": 0.1
  },
  "observables_provided": null
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_rftim_9site_obc():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: estimated_critical_point, critical_point_error, observable_accuracy, phase_classification_accuracy, noise_aware_performance
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

